Article 12
Empowerment of Women in the field of politics and government shall be implemented through:
a. involvement of women in decision-making at various levels;
b. involvement of women in development planning at various levels;
c. encouraging increased involvement of women in organizations and providing opportunities for women to hold public positions;
d. facilitating women's participation in general elections;
e. self-development through organizations to associate, assemble and express opinions;
f. facilitating human resource improvement for prospective legislative candidates, political party members and/or women's community organizations in order to fulfill women's representation in legislative institutions of at least 30% (thirty percent);
g. facilitating increased political participation of women in legislative institutions;
h. facilitating facilities and infrastructure for women's community organizations or community organizations whose vision and mission advocate for the fulfillment of women's rights in the Region;
i. conducting socialization in order to increase awareness of women's rights and women's participation in the field of politics; and
j. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations and/or forums.

